          "path": "_m/u/1/r/3/bombing-of-braunschweig-15-october-1944-wp/royal-air-force-avro-l.jpg",
          "filename": "Lancaster I NG128 Dropping Load - Duisburg - Oct 14 - 1944.jpg",
          "caption": "A Royal Air Force Avro Lancaster I (s/n NG128, coded \"SR-B\") of No. 101 Sqn out of Ludford Magna and flown by Fg Off R.B. Tibbs as part of a thousand-bomber raid, dropping its load over Duisburg, Germany, on 14-15 October 1944. Note the large aerials on top of the Lancaster´s fuselage, indicating that the aricraft is carrying 'Airborne Cigar' (ABC), a jamming device which disrupted enemy radio telephone channels. Over 2,000 sorties were dispatched to the city of Duisburg during 14-15 October 1944, in order to to demonstrate the RAF Bomber Command's overwhelming superiority in German skies (\"Operation Hurricane\"). \nLeft image:  the Lancaster releases bundles of 'Window' over the target during a special daylight raid on Duisburg.\nRight image:  a fraction of a second later, the aircraft releases the main part of its load, a 4000lb HC \"cookie\" and 108 30lb \"J\" incendiaries.",
          "alt": "A Royal Air Force Avro Lancaster I (s/n NG128, coded \"SR-B\") of No. 101 Sqn out of Ludford Magna and flown by Fg Off R.B. Tibbs as part of a thousand-bomber raid, dropping its load over Duisburg, Germany, on 14-15 October 1944. Note the large aerials on top of the Lancaster´s fuselage, indicating that the aricraft is carrying 'Airborne Cigar' (ABC), a jamming device which disrupted enemy radio telephone channels. Over 2,000 sorties were dispatched to the city of Duisburg during 14-15 October 1944, in order to to demonstrate the RAF Bomber Command's overwhelming superiority in German skies (\"Operation Hurricane\"). \nLeft image:  the Lancaster releases bundles of 'Window' over the target during a special daylight raid on Duisburg.\nRight image:  a fraction of a second later, the aircraft releases the main part of its load, a 4000lb HC \"cookie\" and 108 30lb \"J\" incendiaries.",
